Applies-To: refs/tags/155.0.8059.85
Subject: [PATCH] tls: enable the server handshake padding Chrome gets from its field trial

Google Chrome turns on AddTLSServerHandshakePadding through a field trial and
its ClientHello asks for 4000 bytes. A stock build runs no field trials, so its
ClientHello omits the server_padding extension (0x12e0) and its JA4 reads
t13d1517h2 where Chrome 155 reads t13d1518h2. Enable the feature with the
4000-byte request so the TLS fingerprint matches the browser we ship.

diff --git a/net/base/features.cc b/net/base/features.cc
--- a/net/base/features.cc
+++ b/net/base/features.cc
@@ -992,13 +992,18 @@ BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(std::string,
                    &kEnablePrivateVerificationTokens,
                    "");
 
-BASE_FEATURE(kAddTLSServerHandshakePadding, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+// Nanfu: enable the server handshake padding Chrome receives through its field
+// trial. A stock build runs no trials, so its ClientHello omits the
+// server_padding extension (0x12e0) that stable Chrome 155 sends, and its JA4
+// reads t13d1517h2 where Chrome 155 reads t13d1518h2. 4000 is the length
+// Chrome's own ClientHello asks for.
+BASE_FEATURE(kAddTLSServerHandshakePadding, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int,
                    kAddTLSServerHandshakePaddingBytes,
                    &kAddTLSServerHandshakePadding,
                    "AddTLSServerHandshakePaddingBytes",
-                   0);
+                   4000);
 
 bool IsDnsPlatformSupported() {
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
